Introduction to Computer Science: Understanding what a computer is, how it works, and daily life usage.
What Is a Computer: Smart machine that follows instructions. Electronic machine for input, process, and output.
Parts of a Computer: Monitor (displays info), CPU (brain, processes data), Keyboard (typing), Mouse (pointing/clicking). Others: speakers, printer, scanner.
Input and Output Devices: Input (keyboard, mouse, microphone, scanner). Output (monitor, printer, speakers).
How a Computer Works (IPO Cycle): Input → Process → Output.
Uses of Computers in Daily Life: Schools, hospitals, banks, home (studying, shopping).
Introduction to Software: Set of instructions. Educational software.
Using the Keyboard and Mouse: Alphabet keys, number keys, spacebar, etc. Mouse buttons and scroll wheel.
Introduction to the Internet: Network connecting computers. Information, communication. Safety: not talking to strangers, protecting personal info.
Importance of Computer Education: Digital skills, creativity, and problem-solving.
